# The build context of the app's image (stack/app/Dockerfile, ADR 0030), which compose
# builds from the repository root. An allowlist: everything is left out, then only what
# the build reads comes back, so a new file (a secret, a local database, raw captures)
# never reaches the build by default. Left out with the rest: .env and .env.*, .git,
# .venv, tests, docs, tools (tools/capture/out included), .github, the caches, dist,
# build and local databases.
*

# The lockfile and the project's metadata, with the files the build backend reads
# (readme and license-files in pyproject.toml).
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!.python-version

# The package.
!src

# Never from inside the package: bytecode and local databases.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
